Having heard the learned advocates for the parties and perusing the material placed on record and taking into consideration the facts of the case, nature of allegations, gravity of offences, role attributed to the accused, without discussing the evidence in detail, at this stage, I am inclined to grant anticipatory bail to the applicant.
6. This Court has considered following aspects, NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/9749/2023 ORDER DATED: 20/07/2023 undefined (a) the marriage span between present applicant and deceased is more than twenty years as per the FIR itself;
(b) the applicant though happens to be husband whereas as per the statement of son of the present applicant and deceased viz. Jaydeepsinh aged 16 years, he has stated that the quarrel tookplace between his parents i.e. between deceased and present applicant on account of the witness not going to take agricultural produce and for that as the deceased scold him, the present applicant who happens to be father tried to specify the deceased which aggravated the quarrel between them and thereafter, the deceased was taken to his residence by the brother-in-law of the deceased i.e. brother of the present applicant and from there she had gone somewhere and consumed poison;
(c) there is no suicide note found from the seen of offence;
(d) even the younger son viz. Pradipsinh also has given a statement in line with the elder son viz.
Jaydipsinh which is referred herein above, which would NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/9749/2023 ORDER DATED: 20/07/2023 undefined indicate that the quarrel took place not on account of any serious reason but on account of negligible reason;
(e) learned advocate appearing for the applicant upon instruction states that there is no past antecedent reported against the present applicant.
(f) applicant has shown willingness to participate and co-operate in the investigation;

The applicant is ordered to be released on bail in the event of their arrest in connection with FIR bearing NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/9749/2023 ORDER DATED: 20/07/2023 undefined C.R.No.11206076230166 of 2023 dated 18.4.2023 registered with Vasai Police Station, District:
Mehsana, on executing a personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten Thousand Only)
with one surety of like amount on the following conditions:
(a) shall cooperate with the investigation and make himself available for interrogation whenever required;
(b) shall remain present at concerned Police Station on 27.7.2023 between 11.00 a.m.
and 2.00 p.m.;
(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the address to the investigating officer and the Court concerned and shall not change residence NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/9749/2023 ORDER DATED: 20/07/2023 undefined till the final disposal of the case till further orders;
(f) shall not leave India without the permission of the concerned trial Court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned trial Court within a week; and (g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if he considers it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide it on merits;
10.

